## Overview

The OpenSSL toolkit includes:

- `libssl.a`: Provides client and server-side implementations for SSLv3 and TLS (TLSv1.0, TLSv1.1, TLSv1.2, and DTLS).
- `libcrypto.a`: Provides general cryptographic algorithms, ASN.1 engines, CMS/PKCS#7 processing, and X.509 certificate verification.
- `openssl`: A command-line utility for certificate management, cryptographic testing, and cipher benchmarking.

All patches in this distribution adhere strictly to ANSI C (C89/C90), ensuring 100% binary interface (ABI) and API compatibility with existing applications linked against OpenSSL 1.0.2.

---

## Build Instructions

### Production Hardened Build

```bash
make clean || true
./config shared no-ssl2 no-ssl3 no-comp no-zlib no-weak-ssl-ciphers \
  -O2 -fstack-protector-strong -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2 \
  -Wformat -Wformat-security \
  -DOPENSSL_NO_HEARTBEATS
make depend
make -j"$(nproc 2>/dev/null || sysctl -n hw.ncpu 2>/dev/null || echo 2)"
make test
```

### Sanitizer Build

```bash
make clean || true
./config no-ssl2 no-ssl3 no-comp no-zlib no-weak-ssl-ciphers \
  -g -O1 -fno-omit-frame-pointer \
  -fsanitize=address,undefined \
  -DOPENSSL_NO_HEARTBEATS
make depend
make -j"$(nproc 2>/dev/null || sysctl -n hw.ncpu 2>/dev/null || echo 2)"
make test
```

---

## Automated Patching (`patch.sh`)

To apply all patches and verify markers automatically:

```bash
chmod +x patch.sh
./patch.sh
```

